**Settings:** `inf_flavor=0` | `cutoff=0.20` | `ens_size=20` | 2 cycles

| Variable | Max Error | Units | Assessment |
|----------|-----------|-------|------------|
| Surface Pressure (Ps) | 1.298 | Pa | ~0.001% of total — excellent |
| Temperature (T) Level 3 | 0.007 | K | 7 thousandths of a degree — excellent |
| U Wind Level 3 | 0.003 | m/s | ~0.01% of typical winds — excellent |
| V Wind Level 3 | 0.003 | m/s | ~0.01% of typical winds — excellent |

> **Note:** Errors appear very small because only 2 cycles ran.
> The ensemble started close to truth (copied from `perfect_input.nc`)
> and had minimal time to diverge. Running 100+ cycles would produce
> more realistic error statistics.

### Error Map Interpretation

- **Red patches** = posterior overestimates truth
- **Blue patches** = posterior underestimates truth
- **White** = near zero error (ideal)
- **Scattered pattern** = random residual errors, no systematic geographic bias
- **Vertical striping in U wind** = B-grid grid structure signature

